flag provided but not defined: -no-such-flag
Usage of kload:
  -ack string
    	Kafka offset commit per poll: async | sync | none (Pulsar: Ack per message, none = never ack) (default "async")
  -ack-inflight int
    	cap on in-flight async commits per process (full = block, never shed) (default 256)
  -active int
    	rotate/scatter: distinct entities per second (goload -active-partitions)
  -active-policy string
    	with -dist rr and -active N: rotate | scatter (goload -active-policy) (default "rotate")
  -batch int
    	messages per unit (default 100 in batch mode, 1 in keyed mode)
  -batch-max int
    	if > -batch: unit size drawn uniformly in [batch, batch-max]
  -batch-max-bytes int
    	ProducerBatchMaxBytes (default 1048576)
  -brokers string
    	seed brokers, comma-separated (all 3 private IPs) (default "127.0.0.1:9092")
  -client-log string
    	franz-go log level to stderr: none|error|warn|info|debug (default "none")
  -compression string
    	none|gzip|snappy|lz4|zstd (default "lz4")
  -cons-offset int
    	global index of this process's first consumer
  -cons-total int
    	consumers across all processes (0 = -consumers)
  -consumers int
    	consumers in this process (0 = none) (default 4)
  -create
    	create the topics (idempotent: existing topics are checked, not recreated) (default true)
  -create-chunk int
    	partitions per CreateTopics/CreatePartitions request (KRaft caps a request at 10000 records) (default 5000)
  -create-only
    	create (or wait for) the topics, optionally -warm, then exit
  -delivery-timeout value
    	RecordDeliveryTimeout (Java delivery.timeout.ms default) (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 2m0s)
  -dist string
    	entity picker: rr | rotate | scatter | zipf (default "rr")
  -drain value
    	after -duration, consumers keep consuming this long (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds)
  -duration value
    	whole producing time, ramp included (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 1m10s)
  -entities int
    	entities per topic (0 = one entity per partition, entity e IS partition e; >0 = message key e<id>)
  -fetch-max-partition-bytes int
    	FetchMaxPartitionBytes (default 1048576)
  -fetch-max-wait value
    	FetchMaxWait (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 500ms)
  -fetch-min-bytes int
    	FetchMinBytes (default 1)
  -group-protocol string
    	consumer (KIP-848, server-side uniform assignor) | classic (cooperative-sticky) (default "consumer")
  -group-timeout value
    	give up if the groups are not stable within this (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 3m0s)
  -inflight-per-broker int
    	produce requests in flight per broker (idempotent producers: franz-go always uses 5, Kafka's max) (default 5)
  -linger value
    	ProducerLinger (Kafka 4.x linger.ms default) (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 5ms)
  -loader-index int
    	this process's index (0..loaders-1): the "src" in every message and the rr start offset
  -loaders int
    	number of load processes sharing the topics (default 1)
  -local-src string
    	loader indices running on THIS host, e.g. 0-2 or 0,3,6 (e2e_local = messages from these srcs; default: this process only)
  -max-inflight int
    	in-flight UNITS; a unit scheduled while the cap is full is shed (offered+shed, never sent) (default 5000)
  -metadata-max-age value
    	franz-go MetadataMaxAge (periodic full metadata refresh) (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 5m0s)
  -min-isr int
    	min.insync.replicas of created topics (default 2)
  -mode string
    	batch (a unit = -batch msgs of one entity back to back) | keyed (a unit = -batch..-batch-max msgs of one entity; the client batches across entities) (default "batch")
  -out string
    	write the final numbers + config as JSON to this file
  -partitions int
    	partitions per topic (Pulsar: 0 = non-partitioned topic) (default 200)
  -payload int
    	target JSON event size in bytes (goload's jsonEvent) (default 256)
  -poll int
    	max records per poll (Kafka PollRecords; Pulsar: drained from the receive channel per loop) (default 1000)
  -proc-us float
    	simulated processing time per message, µs (accumulated, slept in >= 1 ms chunks)
  -producers int
    	franz-go producer clients per process (unit u -> client u % producers) (default 4)
  -ramp value
    	linear ramp of the offered rate from 0 (goload's F^-1 schedule) (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 10s)
  -rate float
    	offered msg/s for THIS process, open loop (0 = no producers)
  -report value
    	window line every this long (from the start instant) (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 10s)
  -rf int
    	replication factor of created topics (default 3)
  -seed int
    	RNG seed for payloads, phases and pickers (0 = time based); the process seed is seed+loader_index
  -session-timeout value
    	group session timeout (classic; KIP-848 uses the broker's group.consumer.session.timeout.ms) (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 45s)
  -stable-wait value
    	group stable = every partition assigned and no assignment change for this long (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 3s)
  -start-at int
    	start barrier: start instant (unix ms)
  -start-file string
    	start barrier: after READY, poll this file every 100 ms; its content = the start instant (unix ms)
  -tag string
    	free-form run tag (echoed in the header and JSON)
  -topic string
    	topic name (T=1) or prefix (default "bench")
  -topic-config string
    	topic configs k=v,... for created topics (default "retention.ms=600000,segment.bytes=268435456")
  -topic-dist string
    	topic picker: rr | zipf (default "rr")
  -topic-settle value
    	the topics must stay ready (leaders, full ISR, replica logs) this long (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds)
  -topic-timeout value
    	give up if the topics are not created and ready within this (a Go duration, or a bare number of seconds) (default 5m0s)
  -topic-zipf-s float
    	Zipf exponent over topics (-topic-dist zipf) (default 1)
  -topics int
    	number of topics T (names: -topic if T=1, else <topic>-t<i>) (default 1)
  -warm
    	after the topics are ready: write ONE message without "ts" into every partition (and consume it: Pulsar)
  -zipf-s float
    	Zipf exponent over entities (-dist zipf) (default 1.1)
